{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f17dee61-bebc-4ffb-bf70-185dcbc8970a",
    "name": "Tasks API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Spring Boot `tasks` API (http://localhost:8080).\n\n## First run\n1. **0. Setup**: creates the `userEmail` and `adminEmail` accounts (both get the USER role).\n2. Grant ADMIN to the second account (no admin is created automatically):\n   ```sql\n   INSERT INTO user_roles (user_id, role) VALUES ('<adminId>', 'ADMIN');\n   ```\n   `adminId` is stored in the collection variables after sign-up.\n3. **Auth**: run \"Login — user\" and \"Login — admin\". Tokens expire after 15 minutes; log in again when they do.\n4. Then run *Tasks*, *Task events* and *Cleanup* in order (or use the Collection Runner).\n\n## Authentication\nBearer JWT. Each request uses `{{userToken}}` or `{{adminToken}}` depending on the role it needs. Requests suffixed with (401), (403) or (404) check error cases.\n"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "user@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "userPassword",
      "value": "password123"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "password123"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "taskId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "taskReference",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup",
      "description": "Run in order on first start. See the collection description to promote the admin account.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign up — user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Creates an account with the USER role. Running it again with the same email returns 409 (email already taken).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Regular User\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [201]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([201]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign up — admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Creates the future admin (USER role). Then grant ADMIN in SQL and log in again.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Admin User\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [201]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([201]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) pm.collectionVariables.set('adminId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login — user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Stores the JWT in `userToken` and `accessToken`, and the user ID (`uid` claim) in `userId`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200]));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', JSON.parse(atob(body.accessToken.split('.')[1])).uid);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login — admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Stores the JWT in `adminToken`. The test fails if the account does not have the ADMIN role yet.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200]));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminId', JSON.parse(atob(body.accessToken.split('.')[1])).uid);",
                  "pm.test('token has ROLE_ADMIN', () => pm.expect(JSON.parse(atob(body.accessToken.split('.')[1])).roles).to.include('ROLE_ADMIN'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login — wrong password (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [401]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([401]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
